## What would confirm or refute it

{{ decision.next_step }} A deeper secondary eclipse, an odd-even difference or a centroid shift in new data would refute it; transits at the predicted times with the same depth would support it.

## Limitations

- The fit has a jitter term but no red-noise model, so errors may be underestimated.
- The secondary eclipse is only searched at phase 0.5 (circular orbit).
- A second companion whose period is an integer ratio of this one can hide as a harmonic.
- Only SPOC 2-minute light curves of the selected sectors are used.

